## DRAFTER DECISIONS (D-n; accepted or changed by Tuesday at the stamp)
- **D-1 Fix the crumbs at their owner, `customer/parts.tsx`, with `inline-flex min-h-11 items-center`.** The gate named this file as the owner; it is the project's own 44 px idiom (line 188 of the same frame); `padding` would also enlarge the target but changes widths and the separator spacing. Cost stated, not hidden: the crumb row grows from about 20 px to 44 px, so every customer page's content moves 24 px down (a layout change the gate will see in screenshots; STATUS prints the before and after of one page at 390 and 1280).
- **D-2 Fix the gate-named inline links by measurement, layout only, never a word.** The ticket names "the Tasks and pack links" and says the scope call is not made there; the drafter's default is to build every link the gates named that the census measures under 44 px, and to record a link as declined only with a reason you measured. Other under-44 links the census finds (customer list rows, engagement list rows, report link, overview rows, the picker) are **listed in STATUS under FOR TUESDAY and NOT changed**: they were not named, and rows that are already taller than 44 px do not need the link to be.
- **D-3 `partner/parts.tsx` Breadcrumbs is not touched.** The ticket says "customer pages"; B949 measured the partner screens' own crumbs at 20 px too, and the existing Services row excludes them on purpose. The census prints them if they appear on a customer route; the fix is one line when Tuesday wants it (Q-3).
- **D-4 412 item 1 is a separate commit behind slot WORDS.** The word is already the live menu label (not new), but its approval is not recorded (Fact marks). A separate commit makes the choice free either way: EXCLUDE costs nothing, and a later veto is one `git revert` of that commit. The PR text (Tuesday's) must say the label is the one the menu already shows.
- **D-5 Unit rows pin classes, the browser run pins height.** jsdom has no layout; the unit rows would pass with a 20 px link carrying `min-h-11` only if the class were wrong, so they are paired with the census (before and after numbers) in STATUS, and the plants below prove the rows fail when the class goes.
- **D-6 No Playwright spec is committed.** A committed spec needs a shard (`scripts/e2e.mjs --check-shards`) and would run in CI for every future change; B949 set the precedent (scratch spec, not committed). Say so in STATUS.
- **D-7 Own clone, two commits at most, one branch.** The shared repo lacks `d8981b0e`; a fetch into it would move refs other seats read. A second commit only to fix a row (a forward commit, never an amend). Target READY 150 minutes, hard stop 210 (`npm ci`, build, two vitest runs, a browser census at base and head, whole non-live e2e once, five plants).

