3. **No production, no demo or UAT deploy, no hosted site, no HTTP to any hosted host, no `az`, no Kudu, no docker, no ssh session.** Network: `npm ci` (the registry), the one `git fetch` and the one `git push`, `gh` (`-X GET`) only. The browser census talks to `127.0.0.1` ports in your block only.
4. **No message to any human.** No mail, chat or PR comment; you never open, merge, edit or comment on a PR and never write Jira (reads only, every JQL `project = HPSMPOC AND ( ... )`). No person's name in STATUS, code, test names or the commit messages (say "the product owner"). No decision-card id, `C-` entry number, ticket key or `B###` in changed lines or messages. No Artifact, Docs, publish, decision-queue or scoreboard tool.
5. **WORDS.** The only customer-visible string that may change is the one tile title of commit 2 (and only when slot WORDS reads INCLUDE). Every other word, accessible name, href, order and `aria` attribute is equal to main; prove it by a text-content and `getAllByRole("link")` comparison of the changed components in the unit rows. Test names are plain ASCII and name the rule.
6. **Never skip a failure.** Fix the root cause and re-verify end to end; never `.skip`, retry-to-green, sleep-for-timing or environment-gate a row. **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -d/-D`, `--prune`, `update-ref -d`, `worktree prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `checkout -- <file>`); quarantine to `.tools/b1059/_quarantine/` (the scratch spec goes there at the end of each run). A planted file is restored by `cp` from the committed blob. The one removal allowed is your own `heavy.lock`.
